  {
    "index": 3,
    "hash": "vLEGUd2CmA13b/tga+pODXPMWrk=",
    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-14T12:35:35.000Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "## The generator run backwards\n\nNormally codegen flows spec \u2192 code. `--extract` / `-x` inverts it: instead of generating code the command reads the existing project and writes a **spec document** for each module it finds. The CLI describes it as a \"one-shot migration to documents-as-source-of-truth\" \u2014 the way a hand-written pre-Vetra project becomes a project Vetra Studio can drive.\n\n```bash\nph generate all --extract        # every module in the project\nph generate editor --extract     # just the editors\nph generate processor -x         # short form\n```\n\n`startGenerateAll` builds a ts-morph project over the source tree, calls `extractAllDocuments(project)`, and saves each of `documentModels`, `editors`, `processors`, `subgraphs` and `apps` \u2014 then **returns before `generateAll` runs**. Extract and generate are mutually exclusive within one invocation; nothing is overwritten in `document-models/` or `editors/`.\n\n## Where the specs land\n\n`saveSpec` writes to a deterministic path: `<projectDir>/specs/<subdir>/<kebab-name>.<ext>.phd`, with one subdirectory per kind \u2014 `specs/document-models/`, `specs/editors/`, `specs/processors/`, `specs/subgraphs/`, `specs/apps/`. Directories are created as needed, the name is kebab-cased from the document header (falling back to `untitled`), and the extension comes from each document type's own utils. Every written path is echoed as `Wrote <path>`.\n\nThe per-module `--extract` flags name their target explicitly, so the mapping is documented on each subcommand: `powerhouse/document-model` specs to `specs/document-models/`, `powerhouse/document-editor` to `specs/editors/`, `powerhouse/app` to `specs/apps/`, `powerhouse/processor` to `specs/processors/`, `powerhouse/subgraph` to `specs/subgraphs/`.\n\nThe point of the round trip: once the specs exist, they are ordinary Powerhouse documents. Drop them into the Vetra drive and `ph vetra --watch` picks up changes to them and regenerates the code \u2014 the project stops being source-first and becomes specification-driven, without a rewrite.\n\n_Source: `clis/ph-cli/src/commands/generate-all.ts`, `clis/ph-cli/src/services/generate-all.ts`, `packages/vetra/codegen/specs.ts`, Powerhouse v6.2.2-dev.45._",
        "updatedAt": "2026-08-14T12:35:35.000Z"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-14T12:35:35.000Z"
    }
  },
